Package: xFRF
Type: Package
Title: Explainable Functional Random Forests for Functional Responses
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Ufuk", "Beyaztas", email = "ufuk.beyaztas@marmara.edu.tr",
    role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-5208-4950"))
Description: Random forests that predict a response curve from functional
    predictors recorded on grids and from scalar covariates. Each functional
    predictor enters through ridge-stabilized B-spline coordinates, the trees
    split on the integrated squared error of the response curves, and
    out-of-bag permutation importance is reported as curves over response
    time and as surfaces over predictor and response time. The package also
    computes split-conformal simultaneous prediction bands, the smallest
    change of selected recording times that moves a query to another leaf,
    cross-validation of the forest controls, and the data-generating designs
    of the simulation study.
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 3.6.0)
Imports: graphics, grDevices, splines, stats, utils
